- Corrupted .incomplete blob cleared from HF cache before successful launch.

### IFEval inference — prompt format fix
Raw IFEval prompts passed to Nemo without a completion cue produced 0-word outputs
(immediate EOS) on format-constraint prompts (e.g., no-comma, decorative markdown
syntax). Root cause: Mistral Nemo Instruct receives bare text with no instruction
delimiter and emits EOS rather than continuing.

Fix applied to `ifeval_inference_nemo.py`: prompts wrapped in Alpaca format
(`### Instruction:\n{prompt}\n\n### Response:`) for both base and AISF runs.
Alpaca is the training format used for the AISF adapter, so both runs use the
same format -- a fair comparison. Added Alpaca-continuation trim in decode step
(splits on `\n\n### Instruction:` if present).

NOTE for reproducers: `ifeval_inference_instruct.py` (Mistral 7B) used raw prompts
and produced results because 7B is more format-tolerant than Nemo. For Nemo,
Alpaca wrapping is required. Do NOT use raw prompts for Nemo IFEval.

